I apologize for the incomplete response earlier. Here's a complete Java program that demonstrates how to get methods by annotation:

```java
import java.lang.reflect.Method;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

// Annotation interface
@Retention(RetentionPolicy.RUNTIME)
@interface MyAnnotation {
    String value();
}

// GraphQLDirective class
@Target(ElementType.METHOD)
@Retention(RetentionPolicy.RUNTIME)
@interface GraphQLDirective {
    String value();
}

public class Main {

    public static List<Method> getMethodsByAnnotation(Class<?> clazz, String annotationName) {
        List<Method> methods = new ArrayList<>();
        for (Method method : clazz.getDeclaredMethods()) {
            if (method.isAnnotationPresent(MyAnnotation.class)) {
                MyAnnotation annotation = method.getAnnotation(MyAnnotation.class);
                if (annotation.value().equals(annotationName)) {
                    methods.add(method);
                }
            }
        }
        return methods;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Class<?> clazz = MainExample.class;

        // Get methods with MyAnnotation
        List<Method> myMethods = getMethodsByAnnotation(clazz, "myValue");

        for (Method method : myMethods) {
            System.out.println("Method Name: " + method.getName());
            System.out.println("Method Signature: " + method.toString());
            System.out.println();
        }

        // Get methods with GraphQLDirective
        List<Method> graphqlMethods = getJavaAnnotation(clazz, "test");

        for (Method method : graphqlMethods) {
            System.out.println("Method Name: " + method.getName());
            System.out.println("Method Signature: " + method.toString());
            System.out.println();
        }
    }

    public static class MainExample {

        @MyAnnotation("myValue")
        public void myMethod() {}

        @GraphQLDirective("test")
        public void testMethod() {}

        @GraphQLDirective("anotherTest")
        public void anotherTestMethod() {}
    }

    public static List<Method> getJavaAnnotation(Class<?> clazz, String annotationName) {
        List<Method> methods = new ArrayList<>();
        for (Method method : clazz.getDeclaredMethods()) {
            if (method.isAnnotationPresent(GraphQLDirective.class)) {
                GraphQLDirective annotation = method.getAnnotation(GraphQLDirective.class);
                if (annotation.value().equals(annotationName)) {
                    methods.add(method);
                }
            }
        }
        return methods;
    }
}
```

In this code, we have two annotations: `MyAnnotation` and `GraphQLDirective`. The `getMethodsByAnnotation` method retrieves methods annotated with `@MyAnnotation`, while the `getJavaAnnotation` method retrieves methods annotated with `@GraphQLDirective`.

The `MainExample` class has three methods: `myMethod`, `testMethod`, and `anotherTestMethod`, which are annotated with `@MyAnnotation` and `@GraphQLDirective`, respectively.

In the `main` method, we use these two methods to retrieve methods annotated with each annotation and print their names and signatures.
